.\" CaptchaRecon man page
.\" Run: groff -man -Tascii captcharecon.1 | less
.TH CAPTCHARECON 1 "2025" "1.0.0" "CaptchaRecon Manual"

.SH NAME
captcharecon \- CAPTCHA and Anti-Automation Reconnaissance Toolkit

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B captcharecon
.BI "\-u " URL
.RB [ \-\-modules
.IR module... ]
.RB [ \-\-full ]
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-proxy
.IR URL ]
.RB [ \-b ]
.RB [ \-\-delay
.IR SECS ]
.RB [ \-\-timeout
.IR SECS ]
.RB [ \-\-ratelimit\-requests
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-user\-agent
.IR UA ]
.RB [ \-v ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B captcharecon
is a modular reconnaissance and analysis tool for authorised web application
penetration testers. It maps the anti-automation defence stack of a target
application without attempting to bypass any CAPTCHA.

It combines four capabilities:

.TP
.B CAPTCHA Fingerprinting
Identifies CAPTCHA type, version, provider, and configuration leaks
(sitekeys, action names) by analysing HTML source and JavaScript.

.TP
.B Resilience Testing
Tests CAPTCHA implementation weaknesses — missing server-side validation,
empty token submission, field removal, low-entropy tokens, and honeypot
field detection.

.TP
.B Rate Limit Analysis
Probes throttling mechanisms, header-based rate limits, and IP bypass header
effectiveness across nine common header variants.

.TP
.B Anti-Automation Stack Mapping
Detects WAFs, bot management platforms, fingerprinting libraries, and
security header gaps by inspecting response headers, cookies, and scripts.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-u " URL ", \-\-url " URL
Target URL. Required. Must include scheme (https:// or http://).

.TP
.BI "\-\-modules " module...
Modules to run. Space-separated. Choices: detect, resilience, ratelimit,
antibot. Default: all four.

.TP
.B \-\-full
Run all modules with extended checks. Equivalent to specifying all four
modules explicitly.

.TP
.BI "\-\-output " FILE
Save a JSON report of all findings to FILE.

.TP
.BI "\-\-proxy " URL
Route all requests through a proxy. Compatible with Burp Suite, Caido,
and OWASP ZAP.
.br
Example: http://127.0.0.1:8080

.TP
.B "\-b, \-\-browser"
Fetch the target once with headless Chrome (undetected\-chromedriver)
before running any module, then reuse the resulting cookies for every
module; detect and antibot also reuse the browser\-loaded page itself.
Requires Google Chrome or Chromium to be installed. Falls back to plain
HTTP requests with a warning if the browser cannot start \(em this never
aborts the scan. Everything the browser instance creates (profile, cache,
crash dumps) is written to a private temp directory that is deleted the
moment the fetch finishes. Does not hide your IP address, and headless
mode is inherently more detectable than a full browser; see README.md for
details.

.TP
.BI "\-\-timeout " SECS
Request timeout in seconds. Default: 10.

.TP
.BI "\-\-ratelimit\-requests " N
Number of rapid requests to send during rate limit probing. Default: 10.
Increase for deeper analysis.

.TP
.BI "\-\-user\-agent " UA
Custom User-Agent string to use for all requests.

.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output. Shows individual pattern matches, script sources, and
per-request status codes.

.TP
.B \-\-no\-banner
Suppress the ASCII banner.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Full scan against a login page:
.B captcharecon \-u https://target.com/login

.TP
Run only fingerprinting and anti-bot mapping:
.B captcharecon \-u https://target.com/login \-\-modules detect antibot

.TP
Route through Burp Suite on port 8080:
.B captcharecon \-u https://target.com/login \-\-proxy http://127.0.0.1:8080

.TP
Get past a basic JS/redirect wall with headless Chrome:
.B captcharecon \-u https://target.com/login \-\-browser

.TP
Deep rate limit probe with 30 requests:
.B captcharecon \-u https://target.com/login \-\-ratelimit\-requests 30 \-\-delay 0.2

.TP
Save JSON report:
.B captcharecon \-u https://target.com/login \-\-output report.json

.TP
Full verbose scan:
.B captcharecon \-u https://target.com/login \-\-full \-v \-\-output findings.json

.SH MODULES

.SS detect
Fingerprints CAPTCHA providers by analysing HTML, script sources, and
inline JavaScript. Does not interact with or trigger the CAPTCHA.

Detects: reCAPTCHA v2/v3, hCaptcha, Cloudflare Turnstile, FunCaptcha /
Arkose Labs, GeeTest, KeyCAPTCHA, math/text CAPTCHAs, audio CAPTCHAs.

Also extracts exposed sitekeys from HTML source.

.SS resilience
Tests the server-side implementation of CAPTCHA, not the CAPTCHA itself.

Checks: missing CAPTCHA response field, empty token submission, field
removal, low-entropy token patterns, honeypot field detection.

.SS ratelimit
Maps rate limiting and throttling behaviour.

Checks: rate limit headers (X-RateLimit-*, Retry-After), hard limit
detection (HTTP 429), soft throttle via timing analysis, IP bypass
headers (X-Forwarded-For, X-Real-IP, CF-Connecting-IP, True-Client-IP,
X-Originating-IP, X-Remote-IP, X-Client-IP, Forwarded).

.SS antibot
Fingerprints the full defensive stack from response headers, cookies,
and script sources.

WAF / CDN: Cloudflare, Akamai, AWS WAF/CloudFront, Imperva Incapsula,
F5 BIG-IP ASM, ModSecurity, Sucuri.

Bot Management: DataDome, PerimeterX/HUMAN, Cloudflare Bot Management,
Kasada, Akamai Bot Manager, Radware, Shape Security/F5.

Fingerprinting Libraries: FingerprintJS, ThreatMetrix, Sift Science,
Mouseflow, Hotjar, FullStory.

Security Headers: CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options,
Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy.

.SH OUTPUT
Results are displayed in formatted tables in the terminal with
colour-coded severity (CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW, INFO).

A final summary table consolidates findings across all modules with
prioritised action items for the pentest report.

JSON output (via \-\-output) follows this structure:

.RS
{
  "tool": "CaptchaRecon",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "timestamp": "ISO-8601",
  "target": "URL",
  "modules": { "detect": {...}, "resilience": {...}, ... }
}
.RE

.SH PROXY INTEGRATION
CaptchaRecon works with any intercepting proxy. Pass the proxy URL with
\-\-proxy. When targeting HTTPS through Burp Suite or Caido, ensure the
proxy CA certificate is installed in the system trust store, or use the
proxy's built-in browser to generate traffic separately.

.SH ETHICAL USE
This tool is for authorised penetration testing and security research only.

It does NOT solve, bypass, or automate CAPTCHA interaction. It does NOT
perform credential stuffing, account takeover, or token replay.

Running this tool against systems without explicit written authorisation
may violate the Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (CFAA), the Computer Misuse
Act, and equivalent legislation in other jurisdictions.

The ethics acknowledgement prompt at startup is mandatory and cannot be
suppressed.

